      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This is actually the stance taken by philosophical schools like nihilism, but many find it a form of deep despair rather than true peace. On the counter side is the concept of \"transvaluing,\" which suggests that even in a universe meant for entropy, we have the power to create private realms of significance and meaning. Since we do not know if any higher laws of physics will prevent this entropy, we do not know if life is pointless, and living without that possibility is enough to make sense of our struggle.",
